modulo `p` yields `c ∈ F_p[x]`. Directly: `binom(p,k)/p = (p-1)⋯(p-k+1)/k!`. This produces `c=x+x^2` at `p=3` and `c=x+2x^2+2x^3+x^4` at `p=5`.

